        "answerKey": "1. **Definition**: The rank of a matrix is the number of non-zero rows in its Row Echelon Form. 2. **Row Reduction Method**: - Perform elementary row operations ($R_i \\to R_i - c R_j$) to create zeros below the pivots. - For example, if $A = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 2 & 3 & 4 3 & 5 & 7 \\end{pmatrix}$: - $R_2 \\to R_2 - 2R_1 \\implies \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 0 & -1 & -2 3 & 5 & 7 \\end{pmatrix}$ - $R_3 \\to R_3 - 3R_1 \\implies \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 0 & -1 & -2 0 & -1 & -2 \\end{pmatrix}$ - $R_3 \\to R_3 - R_2 \\implies \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 0 & -1 & -2 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$ - Since there are 2 non-zero rows, the rank of the matrix is $2$."
