        "unit": "II",
        "question": "Write in detail the different classifications of ore deposits.",
        "answerKey": "1. **Definitions**:\n- **Ore**: Rock containing minerals of economic value that can be extracted for profit.\n- **Gangue**: Valueless waste minerals associated with ore in a deposit.\n- **Tenor**: Grade or metal content of the ore.\n2. **Magmatic Concentration Processes**:\n- **Early Magmatic**: Minerals crystallize and accumulate early.\n  - **Dissemination**: Spaced out crystals (e.g., diamond in kimberlite).\n  - **Segregation**: Settling of early crystals (e.g., chromite bands).\n- **Late Magmatic**: Residual melts rich in volatiles crystallize last (e.g., pegmatites, magnetite injections)."
