        "question": "The most abundant element in the earth's crust is \\underline{\\hspace{3cm}} whereas the most abundant mineral in the Earth's crust is \\underline{\\hspace{3cm}}.",
        "answerKey": "1. **Crust**:\n- Outermost layer. Continental crust is thick (30-70 km), granitic, and light (*Sial*). Oceanic crust is thin (5-10 km), basaltic, and dense (*Sima*). Bounded at base by the **Mohorovi\u010di\u0107 Discontinuity**.\n2. **Mantle**:\n- Extends to 2900 km. Primarily composed of silicate rocks rich in iron and magnesium (peridotite).\n  - **Asthenosphere**: Upper plastic layer (100-250 km) where magma generates and lithospheric plates float.\n- Bounded at base by the **Gutenberg Discontinuity**.\n3. **Core**:\n- Dense metallic center (Nickel-Iron, *Nife*).\n  - **Outer Core**: Liquid metal (inferred because S-waves cannot pass through it), generating Earth's magnetic field.\n  - **Inner Core**: Solid metal due to extreme lithostatic pressure."
